{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789495125,"nonce":"Rx6ySVUw+R7yjts4R6xX5EsKDvQ=","title":"What the speed-center kernels need of the frontend","message":"Run of the harness (crates/zyntax_python/benchmarks/speed) after the time module, `__future__`, nested import linking, chained assignment, list-literal unpacking targets and `sys.version_info` landed. Each kernel's first blocker on zypy:\n\n- fannkuch: a bound method as a value (`perm1_ins = perm1.insert`), then slice assignment with a step (`perm[:k+1] = perm[k::-1]`)\n- float, nbody_modified: run but die with a signal (a miscompile in the dynamic paths: nested tuple/list unpacking in `for` targets, `dict.values()`, defaults naming module globals, `** -1.5`, `//` on floats); to bisect\n- nqueens, richards: \"calling `name`\" (a call through a name the typer does not resolve; to pin down)\n- pidigits: arbitrary-precision int (marked unmet in the harness, since its wrong answer is not printed)\n- spectral-norm: `try: from itertools import izip / except ImportError: izip = zip` (an import that may fail, and a builtin as a value)\n- scimark (five rows), raytrace-simple: the `array` module (`array('d', [0.0] * n)` and friends; a typed list would do)\n- meteor-contest: `bisect`\n- chaos: `operator`, `functools.reduce`, `random`\n- go: `random` (CPython's Mersenne Twister and its `randrange`/`choice`, so the games played are the same)\n- deltablue, hexiom2: class body statements (class attributes), hexiom2 also `io.StringIO`\n- ai: `re`, `string`\n- crypto_pyaes: `codecs`, bytes, `array('B')`\n- json_bench: `json`\n- pyflate-fast: `os`, `hashlib`, file IO, bytes\n- telco: `decimal`, `struct`, file IO\n\nThe harness reports each of these as the kernel's row; nothing is edited to fit. A kernel that runs but computes the wrong answer must be caught: the kernels print times only, so the harness carries an UNMET table for what zypy computes differently (pidigits today) and any kernel made to run needs its answer checked against CPython once, by hand or through a checksum the kernel exposes.","files":null}]}